From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Enrico=20B=C3=BChler?= <enrico.buehler@unom.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:43:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/33] steamcompmgr: take a game out of iconic when input
 returns to it

A fullscreen game that loses input to the Steam overlay can minimize
itself. gamescope fakes the iconic state it asks for and takes a window
out of it only when the focus window changes. The overlay moves input
focus, not the focus window, so the game stayed iconic after the overlay
closed: Wine kept its client window at the minimized 160x31 size, the WSI
layer refused to bypass Xwayland, and the output showed that window alone.

Take the focus window out of iconic when input focus comes back to it.
Stamp pfhdr24.
---
 src/meson.build      | 3 ++-
 src/steamcompmgr.cpp | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index f582609..3396a99 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -206,7 +206,8 @@ vcs_tag = run_command(vcs_tag_cmd, check: false).stdout().strip()
 #   +pfhdr21 — …and a packed RGB capture dmabuf takes a tiled modifier its consumer accepts
 #   +pfhdr22 — …and a planar capture dmabuf exports its chroma plane where the driver put it
 #   +pfhdr23 — …and the composited cursor follows a shape change or a hide, and the pointer bound forgets a closed window
-version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr23' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
+#   +pfhdr24 — …and input back from an overlay takes the focused game out of iconic
+version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr24' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
 
 gamescope_version_conf = configuration_data()
 gamescope_version_conf.set('VCS_TAG', version_tag)
diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index 0a3948c..246f5e8 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -4979,6 +4979,11 @@ void xwayland_ctx_t::DetermineAndApplyFocus( const std::vector< steamcompmgr_win
 			// don't care if we change kb focus window due to that happening when
 			// going from override -> focus and we don't want to hide then as it's probably a dropdown.
 			ctx->cursor->hide();
+
+			// Input back from an overlay reactivates a game that minimized itself when it lost
+			// focus to it. Take it out of iconic, as a focus change does; never put it back.
+			if ( inputFocus == ctx->focus.focusWindow )
+				set_wm_state( ctx, inputFocus->xwayland().id, ICCCM_NORMAL_STATE );
 		}
 
 		ctx->focus.inputFocusWindow = inputFocus;
